  "description": "VUCZUS crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group I 4 2 2. Reported CIF formula moiety: C133 H132 Br16 Dy4 O43 P8 2-,2(C4 H12 N1 1+),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 14 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 14 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 14 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 14 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 16 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 16 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 16 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 16 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 8 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.674-4.676 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 132.59-136.32°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Me4N]2[Dy4(μ2-η1:η1-PO2R2)8(η2-CO2But)4(μ4-CO3)]·H2O (R = CH(OH)PhBr); anal. Br16C141Dy4H158N2O44P8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
